From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:10:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 154/154] remoteproc: samsung_shannon_cp: sketch of the Exynos
 9810 modem driver

The Galaxy Tab Active3 LTE (SM-T575) has the Exynos 9810's own LTE modem,
a Shannon CP that shares DRAM with the AP, talks through the MCU_IPC
mailbox, and is powered and started through PMU registers and EL3 (SMC
0x82000700) after it has checked the firmware's signatures.

This is the outline of a mainline-shaped driver for it: a remoteproc that
maps the CP's reserved memory write-combined, checks and parses the
firmware's table of contents and copies BOOT and MAIN into place. It
cannot start the CP: prepare and start refuse unless experimental_boot
is set, and start is a documented TODO list. Nothing enables it.

Facts and sources: docs/re/modem.md in the port repository (Samsung's
GPL modem_v1, mcu_ipc and pmu-cp drivers for the same SoC).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/Kconfig              |  11 +
 drivers/remoteproc/Makefile             |   1 +
 drivers/remoteproc/samsung_shannon_cp.c | 301 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 313 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/remoteproc/samsung_shannon_cp.c

